      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Avulsion of a supraspinous ligament is one potential cause of low back pain. Since the symptom pattern of this condition may mimic that of other, more common, conditions, a thorough biomechanical and radiological examination is necessary to ensure proper and successful management. The necessity for a thorough and complete biomechanical, laboratory and x-ray evaluation is emphasized before successful treatment can be initiated."},
